Root cause: Multiple navigation listeners accumulating due to not removing previous keydown listener on each compose, causing focus index to be offset and wrong selection on Enter.

Repair strategy: Before adding a new navigation listener in navigationController.navigate, remove any previously stored listener using a config property (_navListener).

Expected accessibility effect: Ensures that only one keydown listener manages focus, so arrow keys and Enter correctly operate on the currently highlighted suggestion, preserving combobox behavior.

Functional risks: Potential loss of navigation listener if config._navListener is not cleared elsewhere; possible memory leak if not cleaned; but low risk.

Verification requirements: Verify that after typing a query and pressing ArrowDown then Enter, the selected suggestion matches the highlighted item; verify that only one keydown listener is present on the input field; verify that arrow keys still move focus and wrap correctly.

